                    \&amp;\stackrel{\frac{1}{6}\hat \mathbf{p}_2}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^7 U(1))
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the right vertical morphism is a choice of (any) one point in each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              (differential cohomology class) of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 7
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}^7 U(1))
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
              is independent of this choice).
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In terms of local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
              data this has been considered in (
              %a{:href => "#SSSIII"}> SSSIII
              ), as we shall discuss
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#ChernWeilTheory"} below
          %h2#ChernWeilTheory
            Construction in terms of
            = succeed "-Cech" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            We use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            (as described there) by the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msubsup
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mi smooth
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi proj
                      %mo ,
                      %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
            to give an explicit construction of twisted differential fivebrane structures in terms of
            = succeed "-cocycles" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
          %p
            Recall the following fact from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory+in+Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Chern-Weil theory in Smooth∞Grpd
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS"}> FSS
            ).
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The differential second fractional Pontryagin class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 6
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{6} \hat \mathbf{p}_2
              is presented in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi smooth
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              by the top morphism of simplicial presheaves in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi cosk
                              %mn 7
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔰𝔬
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi ChW
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi μ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi cs
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 7
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mrow
                                %mi ChW
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi cosk
                              %mn 7
                            %mi exp
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi 𝔰𝔬
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi diff
                                %mo ,
                                %mi smp
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi exp
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi μ
                                %mo ,
                                %mi cs
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 7
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mi smp
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mi String
                              %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{cosk}_7\exp(\mathfrak{so})_{ChW,smp}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(\mu, cs)}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^7 \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}_{ChW,smp}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{cosk}_7\exp(\mathfrak{so})_{diff,smp}
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(\mu, cs)}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B}^7 \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z}_{smp}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}String_{c}
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            Here the middle morphism is the direct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cocycle
            while the top morphisms is its restriction to coefficients for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+an+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} ∞-connections
          %p
            In order to compute the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 6
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{6}\hat \mathbf{p}_2
            we now find a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            of this morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi cs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mu,cs)
            by a fibration in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi smooth
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            then also the hom of any cofibrant object into this morphism, computing the cocycle
            = succeed "-groupoids," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
          %h3#presentation_of_the_differential_class_by_a_fibration Presentation of the differential class by a fibration
          %p (…)
          %p
            The discussion is analogous to that at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+structure"} fivebrane structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structure"} twisted differential c-structure
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differential string structure
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
                %li
                  %p
                    %strong differential fivebrane structure
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+T-duality"} differential T-duality
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The local data for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} ∞-Lie algebra valued differential forms
            for the description of twisted differential fivebrane structures as above was given in
          %ul
            %li#SSSIII
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "." do
                %em Twisted differential string and fivebrane structures
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001"} arXiv:0910.4001
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-012-1510-3"} doi
          %p The full Cech-Deligne cocycles induced by this and their homotopy fibers were discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
          %p A general discussion is at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
          %p in section 4.2.
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
